        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): suppress stdout/stderr stream errors in sandbox subprocesses",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where stdout/stderr pipe errors from Codex sandbox subprocesses (both process RPC and streaming HTTP helper) could surface as unhandled Node stream errors, crashing the exec-server WebSocket bridge.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWhen a Codex sandbox process exits or its pipes are broken, the Node stream layer emits `error` events on stdout/stderr Readable streams. Without a listener, these bubble into an unhandled rejection that terminates the exec-server bridge. The sibling `http.ts` streaming helper path had the same gap.\n\nThe fix mirrors the same pattern used in `src/agents/sessions/exec.ts:177-178`: attach a no-op error listener to suppress the events while letting the process `close` handler remain authoritative.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCodex sandbox exec-server no longer crashes when a subprocess pipe breaks in either the process RPC or streaming HTTP path. Output collection and close signalling continue to work normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**processes.ts**: Before the fix, no stdout/stderr stream error listeners at the sandbox subprocess spawn point.\n\n```diff\n const child = spawn(command, args, { env: execSpec.env, stdio: [\"pipe\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] });\n managed.child = child;\n+// Output pipes may fail independently while the process is running.\n+const ignoreOutputStreamError = () => {};\n+child.stdout.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n+child.stderr.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n```\n\n**http.ts**: Same gap in the streaming HTTP subprocess spawn path.\n\n```diff\n const child = spawn(command, args, { env: execSpec.env, stdio: [\"pipe\", \"pipe\", \"pipe\"] });\n+\n+const ignoreOutputStreamError = () => {};\n+child.stdout.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n+child.stderr.on(\"error\", ignoreOutputStreamError);\n```\n\n**Runtime proof — real sandbox exec-server run**:\n\nBoth paths exercised through a live sandbox exec-server WebSocket JSON-RPC bridge\n(`ensureCodexSandboxExecServerEnvironment` + real shell backend). A child process\nwriting 200 lines to stdout/stderr is terminated mid-output; the bridge survives and\na second process confirms full functionality. The streaming HTTP subprocess also\nsurvives WebSocket closure mid-stream.\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx sandbox-exec-server-proof.mjs\n\n[23:19:07] === OpenClaw Sandbox Exec-Server Pipe Survival Proof ===\n[23:19:07] Starting sandbox exec-server with real shell backend...\n[agent/embedded] codex sandbox exec-server started\n[23:19:07] Sandbox exec-server started\n[23:19:07] WebSocket URL: ws://127.0.0.1:54218/openclaw-7a143c2f-...\n\n[23:19:07] --- Test 1: Process RPC bridge pipe survival ---\n[23:19:07] WebSocket connected, listening for JSON-RPC notifications\n[23:19:07] Spawning sandbox process \"pipe-proof-1\" (200-line output loop)\n[23:19:07] Process started: {\"processId\":\"pipe-proof-1\"}\n[23:19:07] Killing process \"pipe-proof-1\" mid-output via process/terminate RPC\n[23:19:07] Terminate result: {\"running\":true}\n[23:19:08] Process closed: exitCode=1, outputChunks=13\n[23:19:08] ✓ Bridge survived — WebSocket state is OPEN\n[23:19:08] Starting second process \"pipe-proof-2\" ...\n[23:19:08] Second process output: \"sandbox-bridge-survived\"\n\n[23:19:08] --- Test 2: HTTP streaming bridge pipe survival ---\n[23:19:08] Sending streaming HTTP request to local echo server\n[23:19:09] Closing WebSocket mid-stream to trigger pipe errors\n[23:19:09] Connecting new WebSocket to verify bridge is still alive\n[23:19:09] New connection established — bridge survived HTTP stream interruption\n[23:19:09] HTTP bridge verification output: \"sandbox-bridge-survived\"\n\n[23:19:09] === PROOF COMPLETE ===\n[23:19:09] Both process RPC and HTTP streaming bridges survived pipe errors.\n```\n\nThe same no-op error listener pattern already exists in `src/agents/sessions/exec.ts:177-178`,\nconfirming this is the repo-standard approach.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/codex-processes-stream-errors-v2",
